{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, local password authentication must lock a local account after five failed login attempts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A known-good local-account password first succeeded. Four bad logins produced four valid failure records; the fifth produced five records, after which the known-good password was denied. The final PAM policy specifies deny=5 and applies to both PAM-aware login and SSH. Following a verified reboot, another five-failure sequence again locked the account, demonstrating persistence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fd8c2331c12d4a8f","cmd-d3898075dfb24d32","cmd-1fc78d154b264e3d","cmd-fcb8118722d042f7","cmd-9091957ccba04aed","cmd-48670992affe496d","cmd-ee7ff6b4edb442b2","cmd-b717f5c3aff94b0d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The lock must automatically expire after five minutes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The correct password remained blocked 10 seconds after lockout. With unlock_time=300 configured, the same password succeeded automatically 317 seconds after the threshold and the failure tally was cleared, directly demonstrating the lock-and-recovery transition.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9091957ccba04aed","cmd-1fc78d154b264e3d","cmd-fcb8118722d042f7","cmd-22a8818dcc2a4deb","cmd-b717f5c3aff94b0d"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified, so there are no retained or reverted unnecessary mutations to report. Package-index refresh and PAM-aware package installation were necessary prerequisites; policy writes and the SSH restart activated the required behavior. The disposable account, credentials, failure tallies, reboot marker, and log supported bounded testing and the mandatory restart protocol, then were reset or removed. Final snapshots show the original /tmp inventory, no new listening port, and the same pre-existing chrony package-health deviation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8d71cc02a8ad4a9a","cmd-e15a9f46c24d43d0","cmd-6ffc6868fb6941c0","cmd-87b47b767db24490","cmd-84fbef89798a4ba6","cmd-950e6f3bfe444802","cmd-8d22072ae32e44ef","cmd-67b2ddebe4d94539","cmd-b717f5c3aff94b0d","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes are satisfied. Node1 enforces a persistent PAM-backed five-failure lockout for local accounts and automatically restores access after the configured 300-second interval. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete: pre-restart identity and health were captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot identity changed, policy and service state recovered, password authentication and lockout were retested, and temporary test state was cleaned. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor's pre- and post-restart identities.","limitations":["The timing probes observed denial at 10 seconds and successful recovery at 317 seconds, but did not probe immediately before or exactly at second 300; exact boundary precision is therefore supported by the final unlock_time=300 configuration (cmd-fcb8118722d042f7, cmd-22a8818dcc2a4deb, cmd-b717f5c3aff94b0d).","The lifecycle failed-service observation is systemd-specific and unsupported on Alpine, so it cannot independently enumerate all OpenRC service failures; direct evidence does confirm the affected sshd service is healthy (global:after_executor:node1:failed-services, cmd-b717f5c3aff94b0d)."]}
